age (an init container never names it), `containers[*].ports[*].containerPort` and `spec.ports[*].port`; the variant is the RELEASE ROOT a `# Source:` header names (one release, not one variant per template dir), else the directory (alternative deployments stay apart); peers from env and `envFrom` ConfigMaps — `*_SERVICE_ADDR` and URL hosts by EXACT equality with a Service name or its `<svc>.<ns>.svc[.cluster.local]` form — an edge, or a `dangling` one-sided declaration (not automatically a bug); a dotted external host is a counted frontier, `localhost` / a bind address no peer, shell URLs and embedded ConfigMap documents counted not read; a templated document is refused (with a \"render it\" hint under a chart root), an empty render is not; services declared only by untracked files are named. `s.services_map`, `s.dangling`, `s.external`. Measured on the design corpus's rendered-chart fixture (tests/fixtures/k8s-rendered-chart): every arm at its want — 5 edges, 5 dangling, 0 refused. CART-0830 |\n","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"}},"verb":"edit"}],"explained":23482,"commit":"d1cb3987c07348bfb82b103738cc360c6526eca6","hand":0,"open_intents":[]}
